ASoC: codecs: add SIA8159 speaker amplifier driver

The SIA8159 is a mono class-D amplifier with an analog input and an I2C
control port; on the Xiaomi Redmi Note 12 5G (sunstone) it is fed by the
WCD9370's AUX output. It has no digital audio interface but registers a
DAI so it can sit on the DAI link that drives that output and be switched by
the stream's mute: on at the end of prepare, off at the start of hw_free.
When the DSP port and the SoundWire stream stop, the line output jumps, and
an amplifier that is still on makes a loud pop of it; switching it off first
avoids that (checked by ear on sunstone).

Register values, the chip ID ranges, the on/off sequences and the trimming
check follow the vendor's sia81xx driver (playback scene).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

